§ `Telecommunications Act 2001 — the nouns`

§§ `Copper withdrawal (ss 69AC-69AE, Schedule 2A)`

DECLARE `Copper service` HAS
    -- s 69AC(1) or s 69AD(1) applies to the service.
    `section 69AC or 69AD applies`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copper withdrawal code is approved`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `Chorus complies with the code for this service`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 69AC(2)(b): disconnection the end-user chose, other than temporary.
    `the end-user chose permanent disconnection`        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Schedule 2A cl 1(3).
    `the end-user can access a fibre service`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `fibre installed in reasonable time at no cost`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable notice given to end-user, access seeker and fibre provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the functionality is available over fibre`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `withdrawal and power-failure information given`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `any anchor service is available`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Commission 111 contact code is in force`         IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Disputes (ss 241-244)`

DECLARE `Dispute party` HAS
    `a scheme member`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `determination notified on`                         IS A DATE
    `appeal lodged on`                                  IS A DATE
    -- s 244(1)(a): any further time the court allows.
    `further time allowed by the court until`           IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `Levy (s 14)`

DECLARE `Levy payment` HAS
    `levy due on`                                       IS A DATE
    `levy unpaid`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `levy paid on`                                      IS A DATE
